{"author":{"id":"1d5f412cdeafe9987ad9876b0995bf5032718543d34c038a50cdb41808e9874c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788305135,"nonce":"V9bHQ9adYzAa1R5OkXUHbHA+mbE=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOULVc1M8AAAABPPhjwA","github-url":"https://github.com/kanya-approve/torram-ng/issues/17","origin":"github"},"title":"--symlink is documented and parsed but never implemented","message":"`--symlink` is declared in the argument parser and described in both `--help` and the README, with a warning about data loss. `args.symlink` is never read anywhere in the program.\n\nUsers who pass it get a full byte-for-byte copy while believing they created symlinks — the opposite of the disk-space outcome they asked for.\n\nEither implement it or remove it. A `--link={reflink,hard,sym,copy}` option would be the more useful shape, since reflinks give the space saving without the aliasing hazard on filesystems that support them.","files":null}]}